<feature_description encoding="literal-redacted">
# sh-to-py C1b: review findings pipeline

Part of the sh-to-py bash-to-Python migration (umbrella tracking issue links all parts).

**Goal**: Port the /review findings pipeline: context gathering, panel dispatch, finding collection, aggregation, code-vote tally, tally emission.

**Absorbs (approx lines)**: skills/review/scripts/review-core.sh (958; 3 .md refs), gather-context (84), dispatch-panel (512), collect-findings (514), check-reviewer-failure-threshold (262), aggregate-findings (991), tally-code-votes (834; 4 .md refs), emit-tally (207), log-phase (52; 3 .md refs); scripts/compose-review-findings.sh (350).

**Notes**: /review SKILL.md Steps 1-3 cut over to direct CLI calls; the --subagent SendMessage contract is unchanged. Harnesses test-review-core.sh, test-aggregate-findings.sh (1936), test-tally-code-votes.sh, test-dispatch-panel.sh, test-collect-findings.sh, test-compose-review-findings.sh port to pytest here.

**Dependencies (wired natively via /block-issue)**: C1a, B5.

**Definition of done**: importable functions; CLI verbs in python/cli.py; direct call-site cutover (no shims); pytest replaces harness coverage; absorbed bash + harnesses deleted; stale-reference sweep; make lint + py-lint + py-test green.

</feature_description>


